@* PanelSection (owner, 2026-10-10) — the shared titled-panel header treatment the **Content & Resources**
   block and the **Rules** card both wear, so the two cannot drift apart.

   NAME: deliberately `PanelSection`, not `Panel` — `Panel` is exactly the kind of name FluentUI is
   likely to introduce, and a bare `Panel` in this namespace would then collide or shadow. (The
   component was written as `TitledSection`, briefly `Panel`, and settled here.)

   ITS RULE — kept here because it is the thing most easily lost in a refactor:
   **a THIN LINE runs underneath the header, spanning the FULL header row — the title AND the
   `HeaderActions` slot (the kebab menu) — not just the width of the title text.** It is a sibling of
   the header row (not a child of the title), full-width inside the panel's own box, with the margin
   that separates the header from the content beneath. Owner-corrected 2026-10-10: the first pass drew
   it as the title's own border, which stopped short of the kebab. *@
<div class="panel-section" id="@Id">
    <div class="panel-section__header">
        <h4 class="panel-section__title" id="@TitleId">@Title</h4>
        @if (HeaderActions is not null)
        {
            <div class="panel-section__actions">@HeaderActions</div>
        }
    </div>

    <span class="panel-section__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>

    @ChildContent
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>The panel's own id (the bUnit seam) — optional, because a caller may already own one
    /// (the Content & Resources block keeps `authoring-materials-section` on its own `<section>`).</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Id { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The header text. Title Case, like every other header on the authoring surface.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Title { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>The id for the title element itself, so an assertion can address the TEXT and the
    /// actions separately — they are distinct elements, the rule the owner asked to keep.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? TitleId { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Right-hand header slot: the kebab menu, a card's Add — anything on the header line that
    /// is not the title. The rule beneath is drawn under THIS too.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? HeaderActions { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The panel body. Wrap it in `<ChildContent>` whenever <see cref="HeaderActions"/>
    /// is also supplied (RZ9996).</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}

